{"time": "2026-06-08T23:22:21", "event": "comment1_written", "user_id": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g003_a01_8b8e6868_004", "post_id": "gdyivkd", "comment_id": "37spegk", "target_author": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g003_a01_8b8e6868_007"}
{"time": "2026-06-08T23:22:21", "event": "comment1_written", "user_id": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g003_a01_8b8e6868_008", "post_id": "gdyivkd", "comment_id": "elsz9rk", "target_author": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g003_a01_8b8e6868_007"}
{"time": "2026-06-08T23:22:21", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g003_a01_8b8e6868_006", "post_id": "ksq6doz", "subreddit": "news", "content": "Honestly, why does every news outlet keep hyping up the next 'game-changing' weapon for Ukraine when the front lines haven't moved in months? First it was tanks, then jets, now it's air defense. It just feels like we're being fed the same hopeful headline on repeat while the actual situation is just a brutal stalemate. Are we just not allowed to admit that?"}
{"time": "2026-06-08T23:22:21", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g003_a01_8b8e6868_005", "post_id": "b1d58dc", "subreddit": "InternationalNews", "content": "The way the media sanitizes the Gaza coverage is getting hard to watch. Every report reads like a corporate press release that went through five rounds of legal review. We are looking at thousands of dead kids and the headlines are still using passive voice and dancing around who did what. It's like they're more worried about avoiding controversy than actually reporting the truth."}
{"time": "2026-06-08T23:22:21", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g003_a01_8b8e6868_001", "post_id": "5m2uy2g", "subreddit": "InternationalNews", "content": "Every time they announce a new military aid package for Ukraine, the headlines focus on the massive dollar amount. But if you actually look at the breakdown, half of it is always 'future contracts' that won't even start production for two years. Meanwhile, the guys on the ground are literally rationing artillery shells today."}
{"time": "2026-06-08T23:22:21", "event": "comment1_written", "user_id": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g003_a01_8b8e6868_002", "post_id": "gdyivkd", "comment_id": "jirhz9p", "target_author": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g003_a01_8b8e6868_007"}
{"time": "2026-06-08T23:22:44", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g003_a01_8b8e6868_007", "post_id": "38xbtd9", "subreddit": "worldnews", "content": "Can we stop using 'stalemate' as a lazy shorthand for Ukraine? It’s not a paused chess game. It's a brutal war of attrition where one side is constantly starved of ammo while the other throws waves of glide bombs and artillery. Calling it a stalemate just gives politicians an excuse to drag their feet on sending air defense and weapons."}
{"time": "2026-06-08T23:22:44", "event": "comment2_written", "user_id": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g003_a01_8b8e6868_003", "post_id": "713qwtp", "parent_comment_id": "y80ducf", "comment_id": "v9awvse", "target_author": "6f3p8d1", "action": "comment2"}
{"time": "2026-06-08T23:22:44", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g003_a01_8b8e6868_004", "post_id": "20htdpo", "subreddit": "worldnews", "content": "sick of everyone calling it a 'frozen conflict' just because the map lines aren't moving. it's not frozen, people are still dying every single day in the trenches while we argue about funding."}
{"time": "2026-06-08T23:22:44", "event": "comment1_written", "user_id": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g003_a01_8b8e6868_008", "post_id": "ksq6doz", "comment_id": "rw0fb94", "target_author": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g003_a01_8b8e6868_006"}
{"time": "2026-06-08T23:22:44", "event": "comment2_written", "user_id": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g003_a01_8b8e6868_006", "post_id": "713qwtp", "parent_comment_id": "iaky7by", "comment_id": "0g1vlpj", "target_author": "6f3p8d1", "action": "comment2"}
{"time": "2026-06-08T23:22:44", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g003_a01_8b8e6868_005", "post_id": "36g185w", "subreddit": "InternationalNews", "content": "It’s wild how fast the whole 'rules-based international order' talk completely vanished the second it became inconvenient for Western governments to actually enforce it. Suddenly, international law is just a suggestion."}
{"time": "2026-06-08T23:22:44", "event": "comment2_written", "user_id": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g003_a01_8b8e6868_001", "post_id": "713qwtp", "parent_comment_id": "y80ducf", "comment_id": "8evxp4o", "target_author": "6f3p8d1", "action": "comment2"}
{"time": "2026-06-08T23:22:44", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g003_a01_8b8e6868_002", "post_id": "joazchw", "subreddit": "worldnews", "content": "Keep seeing people say the US is 'running out' of weapons to send to Ukraine. But if you actually look at the numbers, we're mostly sending older stockpiles that were slated for decommissioning anyway. The money approved by Congress is largely going right back into US manufacturing to build brand new replacements for our own military. It's basically a giant upgrade program for our own defense industry, not us emptying our pockets."}
{"time": "2026-06-08T23:23:14", "event": "comment2_written", "user_id": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g003_a01_8b8e6868_007", "post_id": "gdyivkd", "parent_comment_id": "37spegk", "comment_id": "egoffi4", "target_author": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g003_a01_8b8e6868_004", "action": "revisit"}
{"time": "2026-06-08T23:23:14", "event": "comment1_written", "user_id": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g003_a01_8b8e6868_003", "post_id": "36g185w", "comment_id": "fafdyru", "target_author": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g003_a01_8b8e6868_005"}
{"time": "2026-06-08T23:23:14", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g003_a01_8b8e6868_004", "post_id": "ek5mw6k", "subreddit": "InternationalNews", "content": "Sick of hearing about the 'winter freeze' in Ukraine like the war just goes on pause when it gets cold. If anything, the mud freezing means tracked vehicles can actually move again. It's not some seasonal sport with an off-season, the artillery doesn't stop just because there's snow."}
